US-047 is not complete, so I am not emitting the completion signal. I made no source changes this pass. I only appended a re-check entry to `.ralph-tui/progress.md`.

**Where it stands**
- **Done in the tree:** tile splat stride, terrain pipelines, splat shading, tile coverage/picking/depth/LOD-seam fixture, the 4-frame shadow-map check, and a CPU traced-shadow test. The last full Windows batch passed the gates and the GPU suites except the traced-shadow case.
- **Failing:** the GPU ray-traced shadow for terrain. On DX12 and Vulkan the RT-on frame shows `darkened 0`, with no validation messages. The CPU reference on the same tile geometry does shadow the ground, so the fault is on the GPU side. The lit pass and terrain vertex stage match the static-mesh path when I read them again, so I could not find it by reading.
- **Blocked:** `engine_bench --suite acceptance` does not exist in the tree (it is US-074), so the performance gate cannot close. That means COMPLETE cannot be reached even after the RT fix.
- **Not run:** the Linux native Vulkan GPU suite, because this host has no usable Vulkan device.

**What would move it forward**
1. On the Windows host, read back `RtShadow` for the hill frame, or count primary-ray misses and shadow hits on the GPU. This needs a test-only accessor for the RT shadow target first. The memory notes describe the batch route.
2. Decide whether US-074 should be pulled in ahead of this story, or whether the performance criterion is deferred. This is your call, since the PRD does not list US-074 as a prerequisite.
